/-!
# Cohomology of the projective line

Let `ℙ¹_R = Proj R[X₀, X₁]` be the projective line over a commutative ring `R`
(`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveLine`). This file computes the cohomology of its structure
sheaf: `H⁰(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪) = R` over any ring, and `Hⁿ(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪) = 0` for `n ≥ 1` when `R` is
Noetherian. This is the case `m = 0` of the computation of `Hⁿ(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪(m))` (Hartshorne,
Theorem III.5.1). Over a Noetherian ring it also shows that the cohomology `Hⁿ(ℙ¹_R, M)` of every
quasi-coherent sheaf `M` of finite type is a finitely generated `R`-module in every degree, the
projective line case of the finiteness of cohomology of coherent sheaves on proper schemes
(Stacks, Tag 02O6).

The computation uses the cover of `ℙ¹_R` by the standard charts `D₊(X₀)` and `D₊(X₁)`, with
overlap `D₊(X₀X₁)`. Their rings of functions are the degree-zero homogeneous localizations, which
are `R[t]`, `R[t⁻¹]` and `R[t, t⁻¹]` for `t = X₁ / X₀`. The Čech complex
`0 → R → R[t] × R[t⁻¹] → R[t, t⁻¹] → 0` of this cover is exact: a pair of polynomials `p(t)` and
`q(t⁻¹)` that agree is a constant, and every Laurent polynomial is a sum of a polynomial in `t` and
a polynomial in `t⁻¹`. Exactness at `R[t] × R[t⁻¹]` identifies the global functions with `R` over
any ring. Over a Noetherian ring, quasi-coherent sheaves on the affine charts have no higher
cohomology, so the two-open description of `H¹` as overlap functions modulo differences of
restrictions (`TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsQuotientEquivCohomologyOne`) shows that
`H¹(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪) = 0`, and Mayer–Vietoris kills every quasi-coherent sheaf in degrees at least two.

For a quasi-coherent sheaf `M` of finite type the same description presents `H¹(ℙ¹_R, M)` as the
overlap sections `N = Γ(M, D₊(X₀X₁))` modulo the sum of the restrictions `P` and `Q` of the
sections over the two charts. The module `N` over `R[t, t⁻¹]` is generated by the restrictions of
finitely many generators over `R[t⁻¹]` of the sections over `D₊(X₁)`, and some power of `t`
carries each of them into `P`, because `N` is the localization at `t` of the sections over
`D₊(X₀)`. So `N` is `P + Q` up to finitely many elements `tⁱ • n`, and `N / (P + Q)` is a
finitely generated `R`-module
(`TauCeti.Algebra.finite_quotient_sup_of_mul_eq_one`).

The global sections `H⁰(ℙ¹_R, M)` are the pairs of sections over the two charts that agree on the
overlap. Restriction to the overlap sends them into `P ∩ Q`, with kernel made of pairs of sections
vanishing on the overlap. The sections over `D₊(X₀)` are `R[t]`-combinations of finitely many
generators, and those over `D₊(X₁)` are `R[t⁻¹]`-combinations of finitely many generators, so
`P ∩ Q` is a finitely generated `R`-module (`TauCeti.Algebra.fg_inf_of_mul_eq_one`). A section
over `D₊(X₀)` vanishing on the overlap is killed by a power of `t`, since restriction to the overlap
is localization at `t`; the sections vanishing on the overlap thus form a finitely generated
`R[t]`-module killed by a power of `t`, which is finitely generated over `R`
(`TauCeti.Algebra.fg_restrictScalars_of_forall_pow_smul_eq_zero`).

Finiteness passes to schemes finite over `ℙ¹_R`. For a finite morphism `f : X ⟶ ℙ¹_R` and a
quasi-coherent sheaf `M` of finite type on `X`, the direct image `f_* M` is again quasi-coherent of
finite type, and `Hⁿ(X, M) ≅ Hⁿ(ℙ¹_R, f_* M)` because `f` is affine
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.cohomologyPushforwardBaseLinearEquivOfIsAffineHom`).

## Main results

All in the namespace `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveLine`:

* `bijective_baseRingToGlobalSections`: the global functions on `ℙ¹_R` are the constants `R`.
* `cohomologyZeroTrivialLinearEquiv`: `H⁰(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪) ≃ₗ[R] R`.
* `subsingleton_cohomology_one_trivial`: `H¹(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪) = 0` over a Noetherian ring.
* `subsingleton_cohomology_of_two_le`: `Hⁿ(ℙ¹_R, M) = 0` for `n ≥ 2` and `M` quasi-coherent, over
  a Noetherian ring.
* `finite_cohomology_zero`, `finite_cohomology_one`: `H⁰(ℙ¹_R, M)` and `H¹(ℙ¹_R, M)` are finitely
  generated `R`-modules for `M` quasi-coherent of finite type, over a Noetherian ring.
* `finite_cohomology`: the same for `Hⁿ(ℙ¹_R, M)` in every degree `n`.
* `finite_cohomology_of_isFinite`: for a scheme `X` finite over `ℙ¹_R` and a quasi-coherent sheaf
  `M` of finite type on `X`, every `Hⁿ(X, M)` is a finitely generated `R`-module.
* `genus_eq_zero`: the projective line over a field has genus zero.

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem III.5.1.
* The Stacks Project, Section 30.8 (Tag 01XS), cohomology of projective space.
* The Stacks Project, Tag 02O6, finiteness of cohomology of coherent sheaves on proper schemes.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry HomogeneousLocalization Polynomial

universe u

namespace TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveLine

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R]

local notation "𝒜" => SymmetricAlgebra.homogeneousSubmodule R (Fin 2 → R)

/-- The ring `R[X₀, X₁]_(X₀X₁)` of the overlap `D₊(X₀X₁)` of the two standard charts. -/
local notation "B" => Away 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1)

/-- Restriction from the chart `D₊(X₀)` to the overlap. -/
private noncomputable abbrev ρ₀ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 0) →+* B :=
  awayMap 𝒜 (coord_mem R 1) rfl

/-- Restriction from the chart `D₊(X₁)` to the overlap. -/
private noncomputable abbrev ρ₁ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 1) →+* B :=
  awayMap 𝒜 (coord_mem R 0) (mul_comm _ _)

/-- The overlap restriction of a polynomial on the chart `D₊(X₀)`, whose functions are identified
with polynomials in `X₁ / X₀`. -/
private noncomputable abbrev ψ₀ : R[X] →+* B :=
  (ρ₀ R).comp (awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm.toRingEquiv.toRingHom

/-- The overlap restriction of a polynomial on the chart `D₊(X₁)`. -/
private noncomputable abbrev ψ₁ : R[X] →+* B :=
  (ρ₁ R).comp (awayEquivPolynomial R 1).symm.toRingEquiv.toRingHom

/-- On the overlap, the coordinate `X₁ / X₀` of the first chart and the coordinate `X₀ / X₁` of
the second chart are inverse to each other. -/
private theorem ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X : ψ₀ R X * ψ₁ R X = 1 := by
  simp only [RingHom.comp_apply, RingEquiv.toRingHom_eq_coe, RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom,
    AlgEquiv.coe_toRingEquiv, awayEquivPolynomial_symm_X, awayMap_mk]
  ext
  simp only [val_mul, Away.val_mk, val_one, Localization.mk_mul]
  rw [← Localization.mk_one, Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
  exact ⟨1, by simp; ring⟩

/-- Restriction to the overlap respects the constants. -/
private theorem ψ₀_C (r : R) : ψ₀ R (C r) = algebraMap R B r := by
  rw [← Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]
  exact (congrArg (ρ₀ R) ((awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm.commutes r)).trans
    (awayMap_algebraMap _ _ r)

/-- Restriction to the overlap respects the constants. -/
private theorem ψ₁_C (r : R) : ψ₁ R (C r) = algebraMap R B r := by
  rw [← Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]
  exact (congrArg (ρ₁ R) ((awayEquivPolynomial R 1).symm.commutes r)).trans
    (awayMap_algebraMap _ _ r)

/-- `ψ₀` evaluates a polynomial at the coordinate `X₁ / X₀` of the overlap. -/
private theorem ψ₀_eq_aeval (p : R[X]) : ψ₀ R p = aeval (ψ₀ R X) p :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (Polynomial.ringHom_ext (g := (aeval (ψ₀ R X)).toRingHom)
    (fun r ↦ by simp [ψ₀_C]) (by simp)) p

/-- `ψ₁` evaluates a polynomial at the coordinate `X₀ / X₁` of the overlap. -/
private theorem ψ₁_eq_aeval (p : R[X]) : ψ₁ R p = aeval (ψ₁ R X) p :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (Polynomial.ringHom_ext (g := (aeval (ψ₁ R X)).toRingHom)
    (fun r ↦ by simp [ψ₁_C]) (by simp)) p

/-- The overlap ring is the localization of the first chart ring away from `X₁ / X₀`. -/
private theorem isLocalization_ρ₀ :
    letI := (ρ₀ R).toAlgebra
    IsLocalization.Away ((awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm X) B := by
  have h := Away.isLocalization_mul (coord_mem R 0) (coord_mem R 1) rfl one_ne_zero
  convert h using 2
  rw [awayEquivPolynomial_symm_X]
  ext
  simp [Away.val_mk]

/-- Restriction from the first chart to the overlap is injective. -/
private theorem ψ₀_injective : Function.Injective (ψ₀ R) := by
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with hR | hR
  · exact Function.injective_of_subsingleton _
  let := (ρ₀ R).toAlgebra
  have := isLocalization_ρ₀ R
  have hX : (awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm X ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Away 𝒜 (coord R 0)) :=
    mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_injective (awayEquivPolynomial R 0).injective
      (by rw [AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]; exact X_mem_nonZeroDivisors)
  exact (IsLocalization.injective B (Submonoid.powers_le.mpr hX)).comp
    (awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm.injective

/-- Every function on the overlap is `ψ₀ p * (X₀ / X₁)ⁿ` for a polynomial `p`. -/
private theorem exists_eq_ψ₀_mul_pow (b : B) : ∃ (p : R[X]) (n : ℕ), b = ψ₀ R p * ψ₁ R X ^ n := by
  let := (ρ₀ R).toAlgebra
  have := isLocalization_ρ₀ R
  obtain ⟨⟨a, _, n, rfl⟩, h⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (Submonoid.powers
    ((awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm X)) b
  refine ⟨awayEquivPolynomial R 0 a, n, ?_⟩
  have h' : b * ψ₀ R X ^ n = ψ₀ R (awayEquivPolynomial R 0 a) := by
    simpa [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra] using h
  calc b = b * (ψ₀ R X * ψ₁ R X) ^ n := by rw [ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X, one_pow, mul_one]
    _ = ψ₀ R (awayEquivPolynomial R 0 a) * ψ₁ R X ^ n := by rw [← h', mul_pow]; ring

/-- **Every function on the overlap is a difference of functions on the two charts.** -/
private theorem exists_ρ₀_sub_ρ₁_eq (b : B) :
    ∃ (a₀ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (a₁ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 1)), ρ₀ R a₀ - ρ₁ R a₁ = b := by
  suffices h : ∀ (n : ℕ) (p : R[X]), ∃ (a₀ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (a₁ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 1)),
      ρ₀ R a₀ - ρ₁ R a₁ = ψ₀ R p * ψ₁ R X ^ n by
    obtain ⟨p, n, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_ψ₀_mul_pow R b
    exact h n p
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero => exact fun p ↦ ⟨(awayEquivPolynomial R 0).symm p, 0, by simp⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    intro p
    -- write `p = c + X q`, so that `p · (X₀/X₁)ⁿ⁺¹ = q · (X₀/X₁)ⁿ + c · (X₀/X₁)ⁿ⁺¹`
    obtain ⟨a₀, a₁, h⟩ := ih p.divX
    refine ⟨a₀, a₁ - (awayEquivPolynomial R 1).symm (C (p.coeff 0) * X ^ (n + 1)), ?_⟩
    have hψ : ψ₁ R (C (p.coeff 0) * X ^ (n + 1)) =
        ρ₁ R ((awayEquivPolynomial R 1).symm (C (p.coeff 0) * X ^ (n + 1))) := rfl
    have hp : ψ₀ R p = ψ₀ R X * ψ₀ R p.divX + algebraMap R B (p.coeff 0) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [← X_mul_divX_add p]
      rw [map_add, map_mul, ψ₀_C]
    rw [map_sub, ← hψ, sub_sub_eq_add_sub, add_sub_right_comm, h, hp, map_mul, map_pow, ψ₁_C]
    linear_combination (-(ψ₀ R p.divX * ψ₁ R X ^ n)) * ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X R

/-- **A pair of chart functions agreeing on the overlap is a constant.** -/
private theorem exists_eq_algebraMap_of_ρ₀_eq_ρ₁ {a₀ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 0)}
    {a₁ : Away 𝒜 (coord R 1)} (h : ρ₀ R a₀ = ρ₁ R a₁) :
    ∃ r : R, a₀ = algebraMap R _ r ∧ a₁ = algebraMap R _ r := by
  set p := awayEquivPolynomial R 0 a₀
  set q := awayEquivPolynomial R 1 a₁
  have hpq : ψ₀ R p = ψ₁ R q := by simpa [p, q] using h
  -- reflecting `q` at its degree `N` turns `q(X₀/X₁)` into `(X₀/X₁)^N · q'(X₁/X₀)`
  set N := q.natDegree
  let : Invertible (ψ₁ R X) := ⟨ψ₀ R X, ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X R, (mul_comm _ _).trans (ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X R)⟩
  have href : ψ₀ R (q.reflect N) * ψ₁ R X ^ N = ψ₁ R q := by
    rw [ψ₀_eq_aeval R (q.reflect N), ψ₁_eq_aeval R q, aeval_def, aeval_def]
    exact eval₂_reflect_mul_pow _ _ N q le_rfl
  have hrefl : q.reflect N = p * X ^ N := by
    apply ψ₀_injective R
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, hpq, ← href, mul_assoc, ← mul_pow, mul_comm (ψ₁ R X),
      ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X, one_pow, mul_one]
  -- comparing degrees, `p` is a constant `c`, and then so is `q`
  obtain ⟨c, hp⟩ : ∃ c, p = C c := by
    refine ⟨p.coeff 0, eq_C_of_natDegree_le_zero ?_⟩
    nontriviality R
    by_cases hp0 : p = 0
    · simp [hp0]
    · have h1 := natDegree_reflect_le (N := N) (p := q)
      rw [hrefl, natDegree_mul_X_pow N hp0, max_self] at h1
      omega
  have hq : q = C c := by
    rw [← reflect_reflect (N := N) (p := q), hrefl, hp, ← reflect_C, reflect_reflect]
  refine ⟨c, (awayEquivPolynomial R 0).injective ?_, (awayEquivPolynomial R 1).injective ?_⟩
  · rw [AlgEquiv.commutes, Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]
    exact hp
  · rw [AlgEquiv.commutes, Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]
    exact hq

/-! ### Functions on the standard charts -/

/-- The product `X₀X₁` is a form of degree two. -/
private theorem coord_mul_coord_mem : coord R 0 * coord R 1 ∈ 𝒜 (1 + 1) :=
  SetLike.mul_mem_graded (coord_mem R 0) (coord_mem R 1)

/-- The overlap `D₊(X₀X₁)` of the two standard charts. -/
local notation "W₀₁" => Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1)

/-- The overlap is contained in each standard chart. -/
private theorem overlap_le_basicOpen_coord (i : Fin 2) : W₀₁ ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i) :=
  (Proj.basicOpen_mul _ _ _).trans_le (by fin_cases i; exacts [inf_le_left, inf_le_right])

/-- Restricting a function on `D₊(X₀)` to `D₊(X₀X₁)` is `ρ₀` on fractions. -/
private theorem map_awayToSection_ρ₀ (h : Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1) ≤
    Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (a : Away 𝒜 (coord R 0)) :
    (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 0) a) =
      Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1) (ρ₀ R a) :=
  congr($(Proj.awayMap_awayToSection 𝒜 (coord_mem R 1) (rfl : coord R 0 * coord R 1 = _)) a).symm

/-- Restricting a function on `D₊(X₁)` to `D₊(X₀X₁)` is `ρ₁` on fractions. -/
private theorem map_awayToSection_ρ₁ (h : Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1) ≤
    Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)) (a : Away 𝒜 (coord R 1)) :
    (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 1) a) =
      Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1) (ρ₁ R a) :=
  congr($(Proj.awayMap_awayToSection 𝒜 (coord_mem R 0) (mul_comm (coord R 0) (coord R 1))) a).symm

/-- **Every function on `D₊(X₀) ∩ D₊(X₁)` is a difference of restrictions from the two charts.** -/
private theorem exists_map_sub_map_eq (b : Γ(projectiveLine R,
    Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0) ⊓ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1))) :
    ∃ (s : Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)))
      (t : Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1))),
      (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s -
        (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE inf_le_right).op t = b := by
  -- the overlap is `D₊(X₀X₁)`, whose functions are the fractions of `A_(X₀X₁)`
  suffices h : ∀ (W : (projectiveLine R).Opens) (_ : Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1) = W)
      (h₀ : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (h₁ : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1))
      (b : Γ(projectiveLine R, W)), ∃ s t, (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₀).op s -
        (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op t = b from
    h _ (Proj.basicOpen_mul _ _ _) inf_le_left inf_le_right b
  rintro W rfl h₀ h₁ b
  have hσ : Function.Surjective (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1)) :=
    (Proj.basicOpenIsoAway 𝒜 _ (coord_mul_coord_mem R) two_pos).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hσ b
  obtain ⟨a₀, a₁, rfl⟩ := exists_ρ₀_sub_ρ₁_eq R c
  exact ⟨Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 _ a₀, Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 _ a₁, by
    rw [map_awayToSection_ρ₀, map_awayToSection_ρ₁, map_sub]⟩

/-! ### Cohomology of the structure sheaf -/

open Scheme.Modules

/-- On the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)`, the constant fraction `c / 1` is the restriction of the global constant
function `c`. -/
private theorem awayToSection_algebraMap_eq_map (i : Fin 2) (c : R) :
    Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R i) (algebraMap R _ c) =
      (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op
        (baseRingToGlobalSections R (projectiveLine R) c) := by
  rw [baseRingToGlobalSections_apply]
  exact awayToSection_algebraMap R i c

/-- **The global functions on the projective line are the constants**: the map from `R` to
`Γ(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪)` is bijective. -/
theorem bijective_baseRingToGlobalSections :
    Function.Bijective (baseRingToGlobalSections R (projectiveLine R)) := by
  have hσ (i : Fin 2) : Function.Bijective (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R i)) :=
    (Proj.basicOpenIsoAway 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.bijective
  have hres := awayToSection_algebraMap_eq_map R
  refine ⟨fun c c' h ↦ ?_, fun s ↦ ?_⟩
  · -- restricted to `D₊(X₀)`, the constants `c` and `c'` are the constant polynomials
    have h₀ := congrArg ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE (le_top (a := Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)))).op) h
    rw [← hres, ← hres] at h₀
    have := congrArg (awayEquivPolynomial R 0) ((hσ 0).1 h₀)
    simp only [AlgEquiv.commutes] at this
    exact C_injective this
  · -- the restrictions of `s` to the two charts agree on the overlap, so they are a constant
    obtain ⟨a₀, ha₀⟩ := (hσ 0).2 ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE (le_top (a := Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)))).op s)
    obtain ⟨a₁, ha₁⟩ := (hσ 1).2 ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE (le_top (a := Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)))).op s)
    have h : ρ₀ R a₀ = ρ₁ R a₁ := by
      have hσ₀₁ : Function.Injective (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1)) :=
        (Proj.basicOpenIsoAway 𝒜 _ (coord_mul_coord_mem R)
          two_pos).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.injective
      refine hσ₀₁ ?_
      rw [← map_awayToSection_ρ₀ R (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 0),
        ← map_awayToSection_ρ₁ R (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 1), ha₀, ha₁,
        ← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp]
      congr 2
    obtain ⟨c, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_algebraMap_of_ρ₀_eq_ρ₁ R h
    refine ⟨c, (projectiveLine R).sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq₂
      (homOfLE (le_top (a := Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0))))
      (homOfLE (le_top (a := Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1))))
      (basicOpen_coord_sup_eq_top R).ge _ _ ?_ ?_⟩
    · exact (hres 0 c).symm.trans ha₀
    · exact (hres 1 c).symm.trans ha₁

/-- Over a Noetherian ring, the functions on a standard chart form a Noetherian ring. -/
private theorem isNoetherianRing_basicOpen_coord [IsNoetherianRing R] (i : Fin 2) :
    IsNoetherianRing Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)) :=
  image_awayι_top R i ▸ isNoetherianRing_of_ringEquiv R[X] (chartSectionsEquiv R i).symm

/-- **The structure sheaf of the projective line has no first cohomology** over a Noetherian
ring. -/
instance subsingleton_cohomology_one_trivial [IsNoetherianRing R] :
    Subsingleton (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (projectiveLine R)).obj 1) := by
  let M : (projectiveLine R).Modules := SheafOfModules.unit (projectiveLine R).ringCatSheaf
  suffices Subsingleton (Cohomology M 1) from
    (trivialCohomologyBaseLinearEquiv R (projectiveLine R) 1).toEquiv.subsingleton
  have hacyclic (i : Fin 2) : Subsingleton (cohomologyOn M 1 (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i))) :=
    have := isNoetherianRing_basicOpen_coord R i
    subsingleton_cohomologyOn_succ_of_isAffineOpen M
      (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos) 0
  -- `H¹` is the quotient of the functions on the overlap by the differences of restrictions
  have hrange : (mayerVietorisSectionsDifference M _ _).range = ⊤ :=
    AddMonoidHom.range_eq_top.mpr fun b ↦
      have ⟨s, t, h⟩ := exists_map_sub_map_eq R b
      ⟨(s, t), (mayerVietorisSectionsDifference_apply M _ _ s t).trans h⟩
  have : Subsingleton (Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0) ⊓ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)) ⧸
      (mayerVietorisSectionsDifference M _ _).range) := by
    rw [hrange]
    exact QuotientAddGroup.subsingleton_quotient_top
  exact (sectionsQuotientEquivCohomologyOne M _ _ (basicOpen_coord_sup_eq_top R) (hacyclic 0)
    (hacyclic 1)).symm.toEquiv.subsingleton

/-- **Vanishing above dimension one**: over a Noetherian ring, a quasi-coherent sheaf on the
projective line has no cohomology in degrees at least two. -/
theorem subsingleton_cohomology_of_two_le [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] (n : ℕ) (hn : 2 ≤ n) : Subsingleton (Cohomology M n) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian (projectiveLine R) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (projectiveLine R ↘ Spec (.of R))
  exact subsingleton_cohomology_of_two_le_of_isAffineOpen M
    (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R 0) one_pos)
    (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R 1) one_pos)
    (Proj.basicOpen_mul 𝒜 _ _ ▸ Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mul_coord_mem R) two_pos)
    (basicOpen_coord_sup_eq_top R) n hn

/-- The structure map from `R` to the global functions on the projective line is bijective, as
the algebra map of the `R`-algebra structure given by `Scheme.baseRingToStructurePresheaf`. -/
private theorem bijective_baseRingToStructurePresheaf_app_top :
    letI : Algebra R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) :=
      (((projectiveLine R).baseRingToStructurePresheaf R).app (.op ⊤)).hom.toAlgebra
    Function.Bijective (Algebra.linearMap R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤)) := by
  convert bijective_baseRingToGlobalSections R
  exact _root_.funext fun x ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (Scheme.baseRingToStructurePresheaf_app_top R (projectiveLine R)) x

/-- **The zeroth cohomology of the structure sheaf of the projective line is the base ring**:
`H⁰(ℙ¹_R, 𝒪) ≅ R`, as `R`-modules. -/
noncomputable def cohomologyZeroTrivialLinearEquiv :
    Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (projectiveLine R)).obj 0 ≃ₗ[R] R :=
  letI : Algebra R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) :=
    (((projectiveLine R).baseRingToStructurePresheaf R).app (.op ⊤)).hom.toAlgebra
  ((trivialCohomologyBaseLinearEquiv R _ 0).trans ((cohomologyZeroBaseLinearEquiv R _ _).trans
    (structureSheafSectionsBaseLinearEquiv R _))).trans
    (LinearEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.linearMap R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤))
      (bijective_baseRingToStructurePresheaf_app_top R)).symm

/-- Under `cohomologyZeroTrivialLinearEquiv`, an element `r` of the base ring is the class of the
constant function `r`. -/
theorem cohomologyZeroTrivialLinearEquiv_symm_apply (r : R) :
    (cohomologyZeroTrivialLinearEquiv R).symm r = (trivialCohomologyBaseLinearEquiv R _ 0).symm
      ((cohomologyZeroBaseLinearEquiv R _
        (SheafOfModules.unit (projectiveLine R).ringCatSheaf)).symm
          (baseRingToGlobalSections R (projectiveLine R) r)) := by
  simp only [cohomologyZeroTrivialLinearEquiv, LinearEquiv.trans_symm, LinearEquiv.symm_symm,
    LinearEquiv.trans_apply, structureSheafSectionsBaseLinearEquiv_symm_apply]
  exact congrArg _ <| congrArg _ <| ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (Scheme.baseRingToStructurePresheaf_app_top R (projectiveLine R)) r

/-! ### Finiteness of first cohomology -/

/-- The affine coordinate of the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)`: `X₁ / X₀` on `D₊(X₀)` and `X₀ / X₁` on `D₊(X₁)`. -/
private noncomputable abbrev chartCoord (i : Fin 2) :
    Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)) :=
  Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R i) ((awayEquivPolynomial R i).symm X)

/-- The restriction of the affine coordinate of the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` to the overlap. -/
private noncomputable abbrev overlapCoord (i : Fin 2) : Γ(projectiveLine R, W₀₁) :=
  (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)).op (chartCoord R i)

/-- The affine coordinate of the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` is invertible exactly on the overlap. -/
private theorem basicOpen_chartCoord (i : Fin 2) :
    (projectiveLine R).basicOpen (chartCoord R i) = W₀₁ := by
  rw [chartCoord, awayEquivPolynomial_symm_X, Proj.basicOpen_awayToSection_mk]
  fin_cases i
  · rfl
  · exact (Proj.basicOpen_mul _ _ _).trans
      ((inf_comm _ _).trans (Proj.basicOpen_mul _ _ _).symm)

/-- On the overlap, the two affine coordinates `X₁ / X₀` and `X₀ / X₁` are inverse. -/
private theorem overlapCoord_zero_mul_overlapCoord_one :
    overlapCoord R 0 * overlapCoord R 1 = 1 := by
  rw [overlapCoord, overlapCoord, chartCoord, chartCoord, map_awayToSection_ρ₀,
    map_awayToSection_ρ₁, ← map_mul]
  exact (congrArg _ (ψ₀_X_mul_ψ₁_X R)).trans (map_one _)

/-- The functions on an open are an algebra over the global functions, by restriction. -/
private noncomputable abbrev sectionsAlgebra (U : (projectiveLine R).Opens) :
    Algebra Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) Γ(projectiveLine R, U) :=
  ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map U.leTop.op).hom.toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] sectionsAlgebra

/-- Global functions act on the sections of a sheaf of modules over an open through their
restrictions to the open. -/
private theorem isScalarTower_restrict (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    (U : (projectiveLine R).Opens) :
    IsScalarTower Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) Γ(projectiveLine R, U) Γ(M, U) :=
  .of_algebraMap_smul fun r x ↦ (sectionsGlobal_smul M _ r x).symm

attribute [local instance] isScalarTower_restrict

/-- On the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)`, a polynomial in the affine coordinate is a polynomial in the coordinate
with coefficients restricted from the global functions. -/
private theorem awayToSection_symm_mem_adjoin (i : Fin 2) (p : R[X]) :
    Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R i) ((awayEquivPolynomial R i).symm p) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) {chartCoord R i} := by
  induction p using Polynomial.induction_on' with
  | add p q hp hq => rw [map_add, map_add]; exact Subalgebra.add_mem _ hp hq
  | monomial n c =>
    rw [← C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, ← Polynomial.algebraMap_eq]
    simp only [map_mul, map_pow, AlgEquiv.commutes]
    rw [awayToSection_algebraMap_eq_map]
    exact Subalgebra.mul_mem _ (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ _)
      (Subalgebra.pow_mem _ (Algebra.self_mem_adjoin_singleton _ _) n)

/-- **The functions on a standard chart are generated by its affine coordinate** over the global
functions. -/
private theorem adjoin_chartCoord_eq_top (i : Fin 2) :
    Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) {chartCoord R i} = ⊤ := by
  have hσ : Function.Surjective (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R i)) :=
    (Proj.basicOpenIsoAway 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  rintro a -
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hσ a
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := (awayEquivPolynomial R i).symm.surjective b
  exact awayToSection_symm_mem_adjoin R i p

/-- Restriction of functions respects the algebra structures given by global sections. -/
private noncomputable def sectionsRestrictionAlgHom
    {U V : (projectiveLine R).Opens} (h : U ≤ V) :
    Γ(projectiveLine R, V) →ₐ[Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤)] Γ(projectiveLine R, U) :=
  { ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom with
    commutes' := fun r ↦ by
      simp only [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]
      -- The inherited ring hom retains `toFun` coercions; `comp_apply` instead matches
      -- categorical applications. Normalize these wrappers to use presheaf functoriality.
      change (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op
          ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map V.leTop.op r) =
        (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map U.leTop.op r
      rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
      exact congrArg (fun f ↦ ((projectiveLine R).presheaf.map f).hom r)
        (Subsingleton.elim _ _) }

/-- Every function on a standard chart restricts to a polynomial in its overlap coordinate. -/
private theorem map_mem_adjoin_overlapCoord (i : Fin 2)
    (a : Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i))) :
    (projectiveLine R).presheaf.map (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)).op a ∈
      Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) {overlapCoord R i} := by
  let ρ := sectionsRestrictionAlgHom R (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)
  have ha : a ∈ Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) {chartCoord R i} :=
    adjoin_chartCoord_eq_top R i ▸ Algebra.mem_top
  have hmap : ρ a ∈ (Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤)
      {chartCoord R i}).map ρ := ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
  rw [AlgHom.map_adjoin, Set.image_singleton] at hmap
  exact hmap

/-- **The functions on the overlap are generated by the two affine coordinates** over the global
functions: every Laurent polynomial in `X₁ / X₀` is a polynomial in `X₁ / X₀` plus a polynomial in
`X₀ / X₁`. -/
private theorem adjoin_overlapCoord_eq_top :
    Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) {overlapCoord R 0, overlapCoord R 1} = ⊤ := by
  have hσ : Function.Surjective (Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 (coord R 0 * coord R 1)) :=
    (Proj.basicOpenIsoAway 𝒜 _ (coord_mul_coord_mem R) two_pos).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.surjective
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  rintro b -
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hσ b
  obtain ⟨a₀, a₁, rfl⟩ := exists_ρ₀_sub_ρ₁_eq R c
  rw [map_sub, ← map_awayToSection_ρ₀ R (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 0),
    ← map_awayToSection_ρ₁ R (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 1)]
  exact Subalgebra.sub_mem _
    (Algebra.adjoin_mono (by simp) (map_mem_adjoin_overlapCoord R 0 _))
    (Algebra.adjoin_mono (by simp) (map_mem_adjoin_overlapCoord R 1 _))

/-- Generators of the sections over the chart `D₊(X₁)` restrict to generators of the sections over
the overlap, as a module over the functions on the overlap. -/
private theorem span_image_map_eq_top (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    {S₁ : Set Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1))}
    (hS₁ : Submodule.span Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)) S₁ = ⊤) :
    Submodule.span Γ(projectiveLine R, W₀₁)
      (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 1)).op '' S₁) = ⊤ := by
  -- the overlap is the basic open of `X₀ / X₁` in `D₊(X₁)`, so restriction to it is a
  -- localization
  suffices h : ∀ (V : (projectiveLine R).Opens)
      (_ : (projectiveLine R).basicOpen (chartCoord R 1) = V)
      (hV : V ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)),
      Submodule.span Γ(projectiveLine R, V) (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op '' S₁) = ⊤ from
    h _ (basicOpen_chartCoord R 1) _
  rintro _ rfl _
  have hU := Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R 1) one_pos
  have := hU.isLocalization_basicOpen (chartCoord R 1)
  have := M.isLocalizedModule_basicOpenRestrict hU (chartCoord R 1)
  have h := span_eq_top_of_isLocalizedModule Γ(projectiveLine R, (projectiveLine R).basicOpen
    (chartCoord R 1)) (.powers (chartCoord R 1)) (M.basicOpenRestrict (chartCoord R 1)) hS₁
  rwa [show ⇑(M.basicOpenRestrict (chartCoord R 1)) = _ from
    funext (M.basicOpenRestrict_apply (chartCoord R 1))] at h

/-- The Čech description of `H¹(ℙ¹_R, M)`, the overlap sections modulo the restrictions from the
two charts, is a finitely generated module over the global functions, for `M` quasi-coherent of
finite type. -/
private theorem finite_sectionsQuotient (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    [M.IsFiniteType] : Module.Finite Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤)
      (Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0) ⊓ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)) ⧸ LinearMap.range
        (mayerVietorisSectionsDifferenceLinear M (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0))
          (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)))) := by
  rw [range_mayerVietorisSectionsDifferenceLinear]
  -- the overlap is `D₊(X₀X₁)`, where the affine coordinates of the charts are defined
  suffices h : ∀ (W : (projectiveLine R).Opens) (_ : W₀₁ = W)
      (h₀ : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (h₁ : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)),
      Module.Finite Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) (Γ(M, W) ⧸
        (LinearMap.range (sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE h₀)) ⊔
          LinearMap.range (sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE h₁)))) from
    h _ (Proj.basicOpen_mul _ _ _) inf_le_left inf_le_right
  rintro W rfl h₀ h₁
  have hU (i : Fin 2) : IsAffineOpen (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)) :=
    Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos
  -- the sections over `D₊(X₁)` are finitely generated, and their generators generate the
  -- sections over the overlap
  have := M.finite_sections_of_isAffineOpen _ (hU 1)
  obtain ⟨S₁, hS₁⟩ := Module.Finite.fg_top (R := Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)))
    (M := Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)))
  refine TauCeti.Algebra.finite_quotient_sup_of_mul_eq_one
    (overlapCoord_zero_mul_overlapCoord_one R) (adjoin_overlapCoord_eq_top R)
    (S₁.finite_toSet.image _) (span_image_map_eq_top R M hS₁) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨chartCoord R 0 • y, by
      rw [sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply, sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply, M.map_smul]⟩
  · intro n _
    obtain ⟨k, y, hy⟩ := M.exists_pow_smul_eq_map (hU 0) (chartCoord R 0)
      (basicOpen_chartCoord R 0) h₀ n
    exact ⟨k, y, by rw [sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply]; exact hy.symm⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨chartCoord R 1 • y, by
      rw [sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply, sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply, M.map_smul]⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨y, _, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨y, sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply _ _ _⟩

/-- Cohomology of a sheaf on the projective line that is finitely generated over the global
functions is finitely generated over the base ring, which maps onto them. -/
private theorem finite_cohomology_of_finite (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules) (n : ℕ)
    [Module.Finite Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) (Cohomology M n)] : Module.Finite R (Cohomology M n) := by
  let : Algebra R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) :=
    (((projectiveLine R).baseRingToStructurePresheaf R).app (.op ⊤)).hom.toAlgebra
  have := isScalarTower_cohomology R (projectiveLine R) M n
  have : Module.Finite R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) :=
    Module.Finite.of_surjective (Algebra.linearMap R Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤))
      (bijective_baseRingToStructurePresheaf_app_top R).surjective
  exact Module.Finite.trans Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) (Cohomology M n)

/-- **The first cohomology of a quasi-coherent sheaf of finite type on the projective line is a
finitely generated module** over a Noetherian base ring `R`. -/
theorem finite_cohomology_one [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] : Module.Finite R (Cohomology M 1) := by
  have hacyclic (i : Fin 2) : Subsingleton (cohomologyOn M 1 (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i))) :=
    have := isNoetherianRing_basicOpen_coord R i
    subsingleton_cohomologyOn_succ_of_isAffineOpen M
      (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos) 0
  have := finite_sectionsQuotient R M
  have : Module.Finite Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) (Cohomology M 1) := Module.Finite.equiv
    (sectionsQuotientLinearEquivCohomologyOne M _ _ (basicOpen_coord_sup_eq_top R) (hacyclic 0)
      (hacyclic 1))
  exact finite_cohomology_of_finite R M 1

/-! ### Finiteness of global sections -/

/-- A section over the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` that vanishes on the overlap is killed by a power of the
affine coordinate of the chart. -/
private theorem exists_pow_smul_eq_zero (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    (i : Fin 2) {y : Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i))}
    (hy : M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)).op y = 0) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, chartCoord R i ^ k • y = 0 := by
  -- the overlap is the basic open of the affine coordinate, where restriction is a localization
  suffices h : ∀ (V : (projectiveLine R).Opens)
      (_ : (projectiveLine R).basicOpen (chartCoord R i) = V)
      (hV : V ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)),
      M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op y = 0 → ∃ k : ℕ, chartCoord R i ^ k • y = 0 from
    h _ (basicOpen_chartCoord R i) _ hy
  rintro _ rfl _ hy
  have := M.isLocalizedModule_basicOpenRestrict
    (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos) (chartCoord R i)
  obtain ⟨⟨_, k, rfl⟩, hk⟩ := (IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff (.powers (chartCoord R i))
    (M.basicOpenRestrict (chartCoord R i))).mp (by rwa [Scheme.Modules.basicOpenRestrict_apply])
  exact ⟨k, hk⟩

/-- The sections over the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` that vanish on the overlap form a finitely generated
module over the global functions, for `M` quasi-coherent of finite type: they are a finitely
generated module over the functions on the chart, killed by a power of its affine coordinate. -/
private theorem fg_ker_sectionsRestrictionLinear [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] (i : Fin 2) :
    (LinearMap.ker (sectionsRestrictionLinear M
      (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)))).FG := by
  have := isNoetherianRing_basicOpen_coord R i
  have := M.finite_sections_of_isAffineOpen _
    (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos)
  -- the same sections, as a submodule over the functions on the chart
  let K : Submodule Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i))
      Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)) :=
    { carrier := {y | M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)).op y = 0}
      add_mem' := fun hy hz ↦ by simp_all
      zero_mem' := by simp
      smul_mem' := fun a y hy ↦ by simp_all }
  have hK := TauCeti.Algebra.fg_restrictScalars_of_forall_pow_smul_eq_zero
    (adjoin_chartCoord_eq_top R i) (IsNoetherian.noetherian K) fun y hy ↦
      exists_pow_smul_eq_zero R M i hy
  convert hK using 1
  ext y
  simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem]
  exact Iff.rfl

/-- The restrictions to the overlap of the sections over the chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` are combinations, with
coefficients polynomial in the restricted affine coordinate, of the restrictions of generators of
the sections over the chart. -/
private theorem range_le_span_adjoin (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules) (i : Fin 2)
    {S : Set Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i))}
    (hS : Submodule.span Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)) S = ⊤) :
    LinearMap.range (sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i))) ≤
      (Submodule.span (Algebra.adjoin Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) {overlapCoord R i})
        (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R i)).op '' S)).restrictScalars
          Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) := by
  rintro _ ⟨y, rfl⟩
  have hy : y ∈ Submodule.span _ S := hS ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  rw [sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem]
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem s hs => exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hy hz
  | smul a y _ hy =>
    rw [M.map_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ ⟨_, map_mem_adjoin_overlapCoord R i a⟩ hy

/-- Over a Noetherian ring, the global functions on the projective line form a Noetherian ring. -/
private theorem isNoetherianRing_globalSections [IsNoetherianRing R] :
    IsNoetherianRing Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) :=
  isNoetherianRing_of_ringEquiv R (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (bijective_baseRingToGlobalSections R))

/-- The sections over the overlap that extend to both standard charts form a finitely generated
module over the global functions, for `M` quasi-coherent of finite type. -/
private theorem fg_range_inf_range [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] :
    (LinearMap.range (sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 0))) ⊓
      LinearMap.range (sectionsRestrictionLinear M
        (homOfLE (overlap_le_basicOpen_coord R 1)))).FG := by
  have := isNoetherianRing_globalSections R
  -- generators of the sections over the two charts
  have hgen (i : Fin 2) : ∃ S : Set Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)), S.Finite ∧
      Submodule.span Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)) S = ⊤ := by
    have := M.finite_sections_of_isAffineOpen _
      (Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i) one_pos)
    obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := Module.Finite.fg_top
      (R := Γ(projectiveLine R, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)))
      (M := Γ(M, Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)))
    exact ⟨S, S.finite_toSet, hS⟩
  choose S hSfin hS using hgen
  exact (TauCeti.Algebra.fg_inf_of_mul_eq_one (overlapCoord_zero_mul_overlapCoord_one R)
    (((hSfin 0).image _).union ((hSfin 1).image _))).of_le
    (inf_le_inf ((range_le_span_adjoin R M 0 (hS 0)).trans
      (Submodule.restrictScalars_mono _ (Submodule.span_mono Set.subset_union_left)))
      ((range_le_span_adjoin R M 1 (hS 1)).trans
      (Submodule.restrictScalars_mono _ (Submodule.span_mono Set.subset_union_right))))

/-- **The global sections of a quasi-coherent sheaf of finite type on the projective line form a
finitely generated module** over the global functions, over a Noetherian base ring. -/
theorem finite_globalSections [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] : Module.Finite Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) Γ(M, ⊤) := by
  have := isNoetherianRing_globalSections R
  -- global sections are the pairs of sections over the charts that agree on the overlap
  suffices h : (LinearMap.ker (mayerVietorisSectionsDifferenceLinear M
      (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)))).FG by
    rw [LinearMap.exact_iff.mp
      (exact_mayerVietorisSectionsRestrictionLinear M _ _ (basicOpen_coord_sup_eq_top R))] at h
    have := Module.Finite.iff_fg.mpr h
    exact Module.Finite.equiv (LinearEquiv.ofInjective _
      (mayerVietorisSectionsRestrictionLinear_injective M _ _ (basicOpen_coord_sup_eq_top R))).symm
  -- the overlap is `D₊(X₀X₁)`, where the affine coordinates of the charts are defined
  suffices h : ∀ (W : (projectiveLine R).Opens) (_ : W₀₁ = W)
      (h₀ : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 0)) (h₁ : W ≤ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R 1)),
      (LinearMap.ker ((sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE h₀)).comp (LinearMap.fst _ _ _) -
        (sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE h₁)).comp (LinearMap.snd _ _ _))).FG by
    convert h _ (Proj.basicOpen_mul _ _ _) inf_le_left inf_le_right using 1
    ext ⟨s, t⟩
    simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, mayerVietorisSectionsDifferenceLinear_apply,
      mayerVietorisSectionsDifference_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply,
      LinearMap.fst_apply, LinearMap.snd_apply, sectionsRestrictionLinear_apply]
    -- `M.presheaf` is the underlying presheaf `M.val` of the sheaf of modules
    exact Iff.rfl
  rintro W rfl h₀ h₁
  -- a pair agreeing on the overlap is determined by the common restriction, which extends to
  -- both charts, up to sections vanishing on the overlap
  refine Submodule.fg_of_fg_map_of_fg_inf_ker
    ((sectionsRestrictionLinear M (homOfLE h₀)).comp (LinearMap.fst _ _ _))
    ((fg_range_inf_range R M).of_le ?_)
    (((fg_ker_sectionsRestrictionLinear R M 0).prod
      (fg_ker_sectionsRestrictionLinear R M 1)).of_le ?_)
  · rintro _ ⟨⟨a, b⟩, hab, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨a, rfl⟩, ⟨b, (sub_eq_zero.mp hab).symm⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨a, b⟩ ⟨hab, ha⟩
    exact ⟨ha, (sub_eq_zero.mp hab).symm.trans ha⟩

/-- **The global sections of a quasi-coherent sheaf of finite type on the projective line form a
finitely generated module** over a Noetherian base ring `R`: `H⁰(ℙ¹_R, M)` is finite over `R`. -/
theorem finite_cohomology_zero [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] : Module.Finite R (Cohomology M 0) := by
  have := finite_globalSections R M
  have : Module.Finite Γ(projectiveLine R, ⊤) (Cohomology M 0) :=
    Module.Finite.equiv (cohomologyZeroLinearEquiv M).symm
  exact finite_cohomology_of_finite R M 0

/-- **The cohomology of a quasi-coherent sheaf of finite type on the projective line is finitely
generated** over a Noetherian base ring `R`, in every degree: `H⁰` and `H¹` are finite, and the
higher cohomology vanishes. -/
instance finite_cohomology [IsNoetherianRing R] (M : (projectiveLine R).Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] (n : ℕ) : Module.Finite R (Cohomology M n) := by
  rcases n with _ | _ | n
  · exact finite_cohomology_zero R M
  · exact finite_cohomology_one R M
  · have := subsingleton_cohomology_of_two_le R M (n + 2) (by omega)
    infer_instance

/-! ### Schemes finite over the projective line -/

/-- **The cohomology of a coherent sheaf on a scheme finite over the projective line is finitely
generated** over a Noetherian base ring `R`, in every degree: for a finite morphism
`f : X ⟶ ℙ¹_R` over `R` and a quasi-coherent sheaf `M` of finite type on `X`, every `Hⁿ(X, M)` is
a finitely generated `R`-module. -/
theorem finite_cohomology_of_isFinite [IsNoetherianRing R] {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X.Over (Spec (.of R))] (f : X ⟶ projectiveLine R) [IsFinite f] [f.IsOver (Spec (.of R))]
    (M : X.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent] [M.IsFiniteType] (n : ℕ) :
    Module.Finite R (Cohomology M n) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian (projectiveLine R) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (projectiveLine R ↘ Spec (.of R))
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian f
  -- the two standard charts, indexed in the universe of the schemes
  let U : ULift.{u} (Fin 2) → (projectiveLine R).Opens := fun i ↦ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i.down)
  have hcover : ⨆ i, U i = ⊤ :=
    (Equiv.ulift.surjective.iSup_comp fun i ↦ Proj.basicOpen 𝒜 (coord R i)).trans
      (iSup_basicOpen_coord_eq_top R)
  -- `f_* M` is coherent; instance search does not unfold `Scheme.Modules`, so finite type is
  -- derived from finite presentation on the underlying sheaf of modules
  have : ((pushforward f).obj M).IsFiniteType :=
    let N : SheafOfModules (projectiveLine R).ringCatSheaf := (pushforward f).obj M
    inferInstanceAs N.IsFiniteType
  exact Module.Finite.equiv (f.cohomologyPushforwardBaseLinearEquivOfIsAffineHom U
    (fun i ↦ Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen 𝒜 _ (coord_mem R i.down) one_pos) hcover R M n)

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- **The projective line has genus zero.** -/
theorem genus_eq_zero : (projectiveLine k).genus k = 0 := by
  rw [Scheme.genus_def]
  exact Module.finrank_zero_of_subsingleton

end TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectiveLine
